msgid "Qubes ISO building"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/building/qubes-iso-building.rst:8
#: 03be3076e12e4182a7476e6afecbb467
msgid ""
"**Note:** These instructions concern the older Qubes builder (v1). It "
"supports only building Qubes 4.2 or earlier.The build process has been "
"completely rewritten in `qubes-builder v2 <https://github.com/QubesOS/qubes-"
"builderv2/>`__      . This can be used for building Qubes R4.2 and later "
"versions, and all related components."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/building/qubes-iso-building.rst:11
#: 544e670ee3264af49b228b36f53289e7
msgid "Build Environment"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/building/qubes-iso-building.rst:14
#: ee702d2d78e34397acd73d7c50ac4d5b
msgid ""
"Fedora 36 (and 37) has been successfully used to build Qubes R4.1 with the "
"below steps. Other rpm-based operating systems may also work. Travis-CI uses "
"Ubuntu 18.04 to perform test builds, except it can not test the ``./setup`` "
"script."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/building/qubes-iso-building.rst:16
#: 133d8e6ebe9c4558a3e080d49b40cc20
msgid ""
"**Notes:** On modern Fedora system (like Fedora 37) SeLinux is enforced by "
"default and is blocking the build system. You would get error like “can’t "
"create transaction lock on /…/rpm/.rpm.lock (Permission denied)”. You can "
"set SeLinux to permissive mode with"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/building/qubes-iso-building.rst:23
#: d77f543b9269479fb8e353bbf8cb796a
msgid ""
"In ``dom0``, install the Fedora 36 (or 37) template if you don’t already "
"have it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/building/qubes-iso-building.rst:31
#: 8a8174e3efa1435ab064b4174d010a84
msgid ""
"Create a standalone AppVM from the Fedora template. Set private storage to "
"at least 60 GB if you will be building only the default templates; 100 GB or "
"more if you plan on additional. It’s not required, but if you allocate "
"additional CPU cores, the build process can utilize them at some steps such "
"as the kernel build. Likewise, more memory (up to 16 GB) can help. Last, you "
"may want to disable memory balancing, but keep in mind the impact on your "
"other qubes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/building/qubes-iso-building.rst:33
#: 8588fb9d160d45e8b35b3c8895961daf
msgid ""
"Once you’ve built the development AppVM, open a Terminal window to it and "
"install the necessary dependencies (see :doc:`QubesBuilder </developer/"
"building/qubes-builder>` for more info):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/building/qubes-iso-building.rst:41
#: f166fd9b6309407ea1ac3ba155f08007
msgid ""
"Get the necessary keys to verify the sources (run these and other commands "
"below as a regular user, not root):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/building/qubes-iso-building.rst:63
#: 4f354648ca444508b307d160cf92f938
msgid ""
"**Note** In the above process, we do *not* rely on the security of our "
"server (keys.qubes-os.org) nor the connection (ssl, cert) – we only rely on "
"you getting the Qubes Master Signing Key fingerprint *somehow* and ensuring "
"they match! See :ref:`verifying signatures <project-security/verifying-"
"signatures:how to import and authenticate the qubes master signing key>` for "
"verification sources."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/building/qubes-iso-building.rst:65
#: 6db25fa3012142bfa367920e9f093002
msgid ""
"Now let’s bootstrap the builder. Unfortunately, the builder cannot verify "
"itself (the classic Chicken and Egg problem), so we need to verify the "
"signature manually:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/building/qubes-iso-building.rst:75
#: 2fab6c2ecde249f0acc5008a9761501f
msgid ""
"**Note** It’s very important to check if the verification message contains "
"“Good signature from …” and does not contain “WARNING: This key is not "
"certified with a trusted signature!”."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/building/qubes-iso-building.rst:77
#: 101d8bab6af64f99abadee1761575992
msgid ""
"Assuming the verification went fine, we’re good to go with all the rest "
"without ever thinking more about verifying digital signatures on all the "
"rest of the components, apart from an additional step if doing a non-"
"scripted build. The builder will do that for us for each component, every "
"time we build, even for all auxiliary files (e.g. Xen or Linux kernel "
"sources)."
msgstr ""

